export const title = "RS485 Modbus (Satel)";
export const html = "<h1>RS485 Modbus (Satel)</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3>1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\"><li>AI Bridge firmware version 103813 or later.</li><li>RS485 Modbus relay box &mdash; recommended alarm box model: <a href=\"https://www.satel.pl/en/products/intruder-alarms/abax-2/system-units/acu-220/\">ACU-220</a>.</li></ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>When an event occurs, AI Bridge sends a signal to the ACU-220 over RS485, combined with the video. The ACU-220 is a wireless system controller that forwards the signal to wirelessly connected devices to control them. The advantage of this setup is that the ACU-220 can control up to 48 relays, and because it uses wireless communication, no additional wiring such as LAN cable is required.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:640px;\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 260\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"150\" width=\"140\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2a2f3a\"/>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <text x=\"90\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">EVENTS</text>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"148\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">RS485</text>\n  <line x1=\"160\" y1=\"185\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"185\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"300\" y=\"150\" width=\"90\" height=\"70\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dcefe0\" stroke=\"#7fbf95\"/>\n  <text x=\"345\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#20603a\">ACU-220</text>\n  <text x=\"410\" y=\"175\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Wireless</text>\n  <line x1=\"390\" y1=\"185\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"185\" stroke=\"#2653d6\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"510\" y=\"160\" width=\"80\" height=\"50\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\"/>\n  <text x=\"550\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Relay Output</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"148\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrS\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#2653d6\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>AI Bridge &rarr; RS485 &rarr; ACU-220 &rarr; wireless link &rarr; relay device</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<h3>2.1 Wiring</h3>\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">2.1.1 Wiring ACU-220 to AI Bridge</h4>\n<p>AI Bridge uses full-duplex communication while the alarm box uses half-duplex, so the wiring differs between the two. Follow the steps below.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Connect AI Bridge's RS485(RX+) to RS485(TX+), and RS485(RX&minus;) to RS485(TX&minus;). Call these RS485(D+) and RS485(D&minus;).</li>\n<li>Connect the ACU-220's RS485(A) RX or TX to AI Bridge's RS485(D+).</li>\n<li>Likewise, connect the ACU-220's RS485(B) RX or TX to AI Bridge's RS485(D&minus;).</li>\n<li>Finally, connect the ACU-220's COM to AI Bridge's GND.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 AI Bridge</h3>\n<p>To use AI Bridge with Modbus hardware, complete the steps below. Finish all configuration on the ACU-220 device before configuring AI Bridge &mdash; refer to the Satel manual or FAQ.</p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">2.2.1 Modbus Relay Setup</h4>\n<p>After logging into AI Bridge, click <strong>App Settings &rsaquo; System Event Settings &rsaquo; Modbus</strong> from the left menu.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:320px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\" style=\"font-size:12px;\">\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0;color:var(--text-muted);\">App Settings</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0;\">Explore AI Apps</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0;\">Active AI Apps &rsaquo;</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0;color:var(--text-muted);\">System Event Settings &#9662;</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;\">Event/Action</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;\">Alarm In</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;\">Virtual Alarm In</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;\">Generic Event</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;color:var(--text-muted);\">Video Tamper Detection</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 14px;background:var(--blue-light);color:var(--blue);font-weight:700;border-radius:4px;\">Modbus</div>\n  <div style=\"padding:6px 0 6px 14px;\">Disarm</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<p>Select <strong>RS485</strong> as the transport, then fill in the highlighted values. Each value must match the Modbus settings configured on the ACU-220.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip: the ACU-220 supports transmission speeds from 1200 to 19200 bps.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Enter the following configuration values: for the ACU-220, the function value is fixed at 0x10, the start address increments by 1 starting at 0x0500, ON is 0x0001, and OFF is 0x0000.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip: name the relay you want to use and click the ON/OFF buttons to test it.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note: once the ACU-220 receives the command successfully, the red LED in the middle of the device toggles (turns off if it was on, or on if it was off).</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">2.2.2 Modbus Relay Action Settings</h4>\n<p>To add a relay device registered on AI Bridge to an action setting:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>After configuring an AI app or system event, click <strong>Add Action Setting</strong>.</li>\n<li>Select <strong>Modbus Relay</strong> as the action type.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>Add Modbus Relay Action</strong>.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Index</strong> refers to which relay device (configured in 2.2.1) to control. Choose the output type you want, then click <strong>Test</strong> to confirm normal operation. Once configured, click <strong>Apply</strong> to save.</li>\n<li>Click <strong>OK</strong> to confirm.</li>\n<li>Check the checkbox, then click <strong>Apply</strong>.</li>\n<li>Once configuration is complete, click <strong>Save</strong> at the bottom right to apply the changes.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>3. FAQ</h2>\n<h3>3.1 Configuring the ACU-220 Device</h3>\n<p>To find and configure the device, download the installer provided below. This tool is a zip file containing a Windows executable.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/12jkW5ZT8h_pAkcBEzl7aUMIsm3yfYtkC/view?usp=drive_link\">ABAX2 tool download link</a></p>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">3.1.1 Connecting the ACU-220 to a PC (RS232)</h4>\n<p>Connect the RS232-to-PC connector supplied by SATEL to the ACU-220, connect the other USB end to your PC, and run ABAX2.</p>\n<p>Click the hamburger menu button at the top right, then click <strong>Configuration</strong>.</p>\n<p>Select the port and click <strong>OK</strong>. Clicking the highlighted button at the top right connects to the ACU-220. On a successful connection, the model name and firmware version appear in the green box at the top center, and the asterisk next to the model name blinks. The blue box shows the ACU-220's current state.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip: if you're connecting the ACU-220 for the first time, or an info box shows red, click the yellow box button at the top right to refresh the ACU-220's current state.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">3.1.2 Registering a Wireless Device on the ACU-220</h4>\n<p>From ABAX2's left menu, click <strong>Devices</strong>. Click the button at the bottom to enter the serial number of the device you want to connect (this manual is written based on the ACX-210).</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Tip: the device's serial number is printed on the device labeled \"sn:\" and is 6 digits.</p>\n</div>\n<p>After entering the serial number, a \"Trigger device tamper contact\" message appears. Power on the ACX-210 at this point, and the device is recognized and the screen changes. Choose how many outputs to use and the position to list it in, then click <strong>OK</strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note: if only one position is selected, outputs are numbered sequentially starting from 1.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Once the device is added successfully, click the button at the top right to save. When the save succeeds, the red box disappears.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note: a ^ symbol in the Type column indicates it's the same as the entry above it.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4 style=\"margin-top:16px;\">3.1.3 ACU-220 MODBUS Settings</h4>\n<p>In ABAX2's Configuration tab, check the MODBUS setting at the bottom and choose the values to use. Once configured, click the button at the top right to save.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;\">Tip: AI Bridge supports baud rates from 9600 to 115200 bps.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">Note: the values configured here are used on AI Bridge &mdash; the MODBUS address refers to the Device Address on AI Bridge.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>4. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\"><li>v1.00 &ndash; initial document</li><li>v1.10 &ndash; added ABAX2 tool download link to 3.1 ACU-220 Device Setting</li></ul>";
